y chips away at  loki's resolve  i hope you know you deserve to be alone  and you always will be  the god of mischief has always seen  himself as a loner and an outsider even  though he was considered family by the  likes of thorin odin  obviously this version of the character  didn't get the original story arc after  the events of the avengers that made him  realize that he truly has a family but  this time luke is clearly setting the  asgardian up to realize that he doesn't  want to live like that anymore  additionally loki is falling for sylvie  something mobius finds hilarious in his  interrogation scene  what a incredible seismic narcissist  you felt for yourself indeed loki's in  love with himself a development that  definitely doesn't seem like it will end  well  however loki's conversation with mobius  leads to the god of mischief trying to  convince mobius that everyone at the tva  are actually variants whose memories  have been erased  loki's insistence that timekeepers are  kidnapping variants and wiping their  memories to work for the tva pushes  mobius to look into his claims in fact  it says a lot about the impact loki has  had on the tva analyst that he's started  to take him seriously  mobius and loki have struck up a genuine  friendship even if that friendship is  based on the two of them trying to  outsmart each other at every turn  it's that friendship that makes mobius  sneak a look at ravana's tempat after  she refuses to explain what really  happened to hunter c20  which allows him to discover that loki  was right about the tva  this means ravana is covering up the  timekeeper's deceit  obviously ravana doesn't want this  information to become public knowledge  so when mobius starts wondering aloud  about what his life was like before  being a cosmic bureaucrat she orders a  hunter to prune him  hopefully this isn't the last we see of  mobius  ever since the first episode of loki  fans have suspected that the timekeepers  aren't even real  largely because we haven't seen them in  action at all in the series so far  but in a surprise twist ravana takes the  two loki variants to meet the trio of  space lizards  leading to an interesting conversation  between the tba chief and sylvie  after everything silvia is still  desperate for answers about why her life  was thrown into ruin because of the tva  the show still hasn't explained what  nexus event made the tva go after sylvie  and ravana isn't about to open up about  that just yet  instead she brushes silvie's question  off saying she doesn't remember why they  were sent after her which visibly  crushes and enrages sylvie  after an atmospheric battle in the  timekeeper's smoky chamber the series  reveals the three aliens running the tva  are actually androids so clearly someone  else entirely is pulling the tva strings  but who's really behind the tva  regardless the variants have proved that  perhaps a dash of chaos is exactly what  the multiverse needs  they're even on the cusp of confessing  their feelings for one another a  possibility seemingly ruined when ravana  prunes loki right in front of sylvie  but wait there's more the series first  mid-credit scene reveals that loki might  not be dead  once again the trickster cheats death in  the mcu and the asgardian wakes up in  what looks like a ruined version of new  york asking if he's in hell  in response a dramatic voice replies  not yet but you will be unless you come  with us  and that's when the show's biggest twist  yet is revealed introducing us to four  more loki variants  is this new world filled with other dead  loki's or is it home to countless pruned  variants from across the multiverse  hopefully episode 5 will have more  answers  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite  mcu shows are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one
 

